A thread taken off a ring while it is the oldest stays the ring's head.
The next signal would wake a thread that is no longer waiting,
and the next switch run one that is already running;
a queue holds only threads in the state it is for.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: queue holds a place it is not for
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -108,9 +108,6 @@ static void ring_remove(paddr_t *head, paddr_t self, size_t off)
     } else {
         links_at(s->prev, off)->next = s->next;
         links_at(s->next, off)->prev = s->prev;
-        if (*head == self) {
-            *head = s->next;
-        }
     }
     s->next = s->prev = 0;
 }
